WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.220
The algorithmic capabilities we evaluate
today represent a specific point on a

2
00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:07.280
much longer evolutionary timeline.

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.900
Current foundation models and large
language models sit here.

4
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.340
They show early signs of general purpose
capabilities, able to perform tasks

5
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:19.240
across multiple domains, rather than being
limited to a single function.

6
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.800
This current state must be clearly
differentiated from the theoretical

7
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:27.060
endpoint on the right. Artificial General
Intelligence, or Strong AI,

8
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.260
is a hypothetical future state.

9
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.400
It would be characterized characterized by
true reasoning, consciousness,

10
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.360
and the ability to apply knowledge across
any task at or beyond the human

11
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.520
level. We are not evaluating artificial
general intelligence today.

12
00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.580
When reviewing research proposals, we
evaluate narrow, highly complex,

13
00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.200
statistics-driven data engines running on
physical hardware.

14
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:53.380
A rigorous, demystified understanding of
these statistical mechanics and

15
00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.720
structural vulnerabilities is the non-
negotiable prerequisite.

16
00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:01.260
Without it, proportionate and responsible
ethical review is impossible.

17
00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:04.116
Thank you for engaging with this
foundational module.
